<BaseLayout title="Privacy — SiteRadian" description="Privacy information for the static SiteRadian website and the SiteRadian WordPress plugin.">
  <header class="page-hero"><div class="container narrow"><p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p><h1>No tracking by default.</h1><p class="lede">This website is static and intentionally avoids analytics, advertising pixels, accounts, forms, and behavioral tracking.</p></div></header>
  <section class="section"><div class="container search-shell docs-content"><section><h2>This website</h2><p>SiteRadian’s public website is hosted on GitHub Pages. It does not set first-party analytics cookies, collect form submissions, or run third-party analytics. GitHub may process ordinary infrastructure logs under its own terms and privacy practices.</p></section><section><h2>The WordPress plugin</h2><p>SiteRadian runs on your WordPress site. By default it contacts no external service, sends no telemetry, and performs no licence check. Assistant traffic occurs only after you configure an external client. Optional Built-in AI features contact only the provider you select, for the operation you invoke.</p></section><section><h2>Links to other services</h2><p>Documentation links may lead to GitHub, WordPress.org, or assistant vendors. Those sites control their own privacy practices. SiteRadian does not receive their account credentials.</p></section><section><h2>Changes</h2><p>This notice may be updated when the website or product changes. Material behavior will be described factually in the relevant release documentation.</p></section></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
